Elaine R.: Quick question — I opened PR #428 to add owner labels to projected secrets in payment-service. It's a tiny TF change but worried about secret refresh debounce behavior. Anyone know if label changes trigger ExternalSecrets reconcile?
Matt S.: @Elaine R. AFAIK ExternalSecrets watches annotations + data, not labels. But we recently added pod-level annotation debounce — can someone confirm?
Priya K.: Labels usually won't change the Secret data. However our sync controller sometimes updates Secret metadata (labels/annotations) during reconcile. If it writes the Secret it could bump resourceVersion which may look like a write and trigger downstream webhooks. Need to check controller logic.
Jordan L.: Can you paste the PR/diff? also interested in where you put the annotation.
Elaine R.: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/428 — diff snippet: ```terraform
resource "kubernetes_secret" "proj" {
  metadata {
    labels = {
      owner = var.team
    }
    annotations = {
      "externalsecrets.redwood.io/refresh-debounce" = "30s"
    }
  }
}
```
Priya K.: Note: the controller reads refresh-debounce from the ExternalSecret resource, not the Secret. Putting the annotation on the Secret won't be picked up. Also our controller historically did a full metadata patch which caused churn if TF and controller both touch labels.
Matt S.: We actually saw this in staging a couple weeks ago — adding TF labels caused a ~2s reconcile loop because the reconciler copied metadata even when identical. Filed ISSUE-592.
Elaine R.: Hmm. So immediate fix is to move the debounce annotation to the ExternalSecret and avoid changing Secret annotations/labels from TF?
Jordan L.: Short-term workaround: add a lifecycle ignore_changes for metadata[0].labels in the TF resource so TF doesn't constantly fight controller mutations, e.g.: ```hcl
lifecycle {
  ignore_changes = [metadata[0].labels]
}
``` Longer-term we should update the controller to avoid rewriting unchanged labels.
Priya K.: Agreed. Also ensure ExternalSecret template can inject owner label if you want it tied to downstream Secret without TF touching it. That keeps a single source of truth.
Elaine R.: OK I'll move the refresh-debounce annotation into the ExternalSecret manifest and switch label ownership to ExternalSecret template. I'll also add the lifecycle ignore_changes as a belt-and-suspenders approach.
Matt S.: :thumbsup: Can someone run a quick staging smoke after the PR lands? @Jordan L. can you watch controller logs for 10–15m around the apply (14:30 PT)?
Jordan L.: Yep I can. Will tail controller logs + `kubectl get events -w` and report any flapping.
.deploy-bot: deploy queued: infra/pr-428 -> staging (plan apply queued).
Elaine R.: Thanks everyone — I'll update the PR and ping when it's ready for a re-run in staging.
